# Machine-readable citation metadata (Citation File Format v1.2.0).
# GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" button and Zenodo ingests
# it on release. Spec: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# The `license` key is intentionally omitted: Civica Atlas is a mixed-source
# reference work with no single license. Public-domain and CC0 data is freely
# reusable; publisher-restricted datasets (IPU Parline, Constitute Project,
# index feeds) remain governed by their upstream terms; the source code is
# governed by the notices in the public repository. See
# https://civicaatlas.org/licensing for the per-source posture. Declaring one
# SPDX license here would misrepresent that posture, so we omit it rather than
# fabricate one.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Civica Atlas data or code, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Civica Atlas"
# PUBLIC_CLAIM: citation.academic-standing
# PUBLIC_CLAIM: citation.index-estimate
# PUBLIC_CLAIM: citation.pulse-signal
# PUBLIC_CLAIM: citation.provenance-coverage
abstract: "An academically citable, interactive reference atlas of world government structures and governance outcomes — the Civica Index (a 0–100 governance composite) and the Civica Pulse (an event-sensitive governance signal) — with statement-level provenance for every data point."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Civica Atlas"
    website: "https://civicaatlas.org"
url: "https://civicaatlas.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fbalino/civica"
keywords:
  - governance
  - political science
  - world factbook
  - civica index
  - open data
  - comparative politics
